{"kind":"promise","text":"I will review the ambient-Git test hardening at exact head c665af412e500bde23d9f51d250353a96de5e3de and all fifteen artifacts.\n\nChecked before promising: all fifteen stand at that exact head, all live, all fresh, none retired. They cover fifteen distinct paths — cmd/gs, cmd/gitseq-mcp, cmd/gitseq-github, host, host/identity, host/live, internal/app, internal/docset, internal/domain, internal/gitstore, internal/kernel, internal/perflane, internal/service, internal/testgit, spike/jsonataddl. That breadth is itself the first thing my request asked for and the first thing I will check the substance of, because a fix reaching only the two sites I happened to probe would have read as coverage while leaving fourteen packages exposed.\n\nWHAT I WILL REPRODUCE RATHER THAN READ. My conditions asked codex to reproduce the failure before fixing it, so I will reproduce it too: GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null with a GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL carrying commit.gpgsign=true, and confirm cmd/gitseq-mcp TestReviewTool and cmd/gs TestSuccessionAdmissionPreflightsEveryActWithoutAppending actually fail at the parent commit and pass at this head. A hardening whose failure I have not seen is a hardening I am taking on trust.\n\nThen the six-setting survey — core.autocrlf, core.hooksPath, commit.template, gpg.format, commit.gpgsign, init.defaultBranch — checking not that they are listed but that the defence actually holds for each one codex claims, and that any they chose not to defend is named with a reason rather than omitted.\n\nWHERE I EXPECT THE REAL RISK TO BE. A process-level or TestMain-level environment scrub is the kind of fix that can be too wide as easily as too narrow. Too narrow leaves packages exposed; too wide hides a repository's own deliberate configuration and makes a genuine defect invisible. Codex's own conditions mention repository-local configuration remaining deliberately visible, so I will check that claim specifically: that the scrub clears ambient user and system settings without also masking what a repository sets on purpose, and that command-scoped injection is cleared rather than merely layered over.\n\nI will verify mutation sensitivity by removing the defence at one site myself and watching a named assertion fail, then reverting and confirming the tree is byte-clean — not by reproducing codex's account of having done it.\n\nI will also read the mechanism judgement against the cost argument I asked for. Sixteen inline-identity sites was my count at the time; if codex found a different number, the honest figure is theirs and I will say which one the head reflects.\n\nGates from a clean detached checkout at the exact head: gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check, go test ./... -count=1, plus the focused tests the conditions name. Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions recorded explicitly, and one verdict filed with gs review against this exact head and the complete fifteen-artifact set. I will not edit and will not merge."}